Z||000025||WKDFIRO||11-26-1999||12:33 AM||||I think that, in my opinion, that the "new blood" that GM has put out is not always on the mark. Granted the Northstar/Aurora powerplants are a fantastic step in the right direction, but it will be sometime before it comes down to the lower models. I am forced to consider the demise of the Impala and the "new blood" that exists now. Kind of a let down. GM has yet to show the dedication to its history that say Ford (and I HATE saying the F word) has with its new Thunderbird or Chrysler's 300M. <P>Giving up the Firebird/Camaro should not be so easy. As for the article, the part where it talks about the "plastic surgery" right near a Firebird burnout is laughable. Pontiac has always been on the cutting edge of style. Some like it and some won't but you WILL NOT mistake a Firebird with a Camaro! And I like that.<P>Oh, and Battlestar Galactica was a sci-fi television show in the early 80s taking advantage of the Star Wars craze. I guess the implication is that there might be a movie remake or something of the TV show. I have not heard of this but the trend to bastardize TV shows for movies does seem to be the rage right now. Captain Video...now thats something beyond me.<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 11-26-1999).]||||reg||10
Z||000026||Monkeyman||11-26-1999||12:43 AM||||COUNTIBLIS--try comparing the new camaros to the originals.  They are new blood.  And you are correct.  The Fiero isn't a musclecar.  It was never meant to be one.  It's a sporty/sports car.  (There is a difference).  I hope you won't leave Cliffs' forum.  Nobody's going off the deep end.  I've only been here a short while and I've already found that some of the people here are very friendly and helpful.  <BR>AL--The original musclecar was the GTO and they discontinued that in the early '70s.  And I'm saying that as a 110% American (fought for my country and all that).<BR>four50four-Battlestar Galactica was a sci-fi show on TV about 8 or 10 years ago.  Kinda like Babylon 5.  Basically just a cheap take off of the original Star Trek (the BEST show of its' type!-yes...I'm a Trekkie)  ||||reg||1
Z||000027||RZURCTN||11-26-1999||01:01 AM||||I'm am just happy to see todays car makers coming back to the muscle car.  The economy is good and there is a market for them again.  Remember that the Fiero was originally designed as a commuter car, it had to have great gas mileage and a sporty look.  It wasn't meant to a grocery-getter.  I believe that for what they were trying to accomplish, GM did a heck of a great job.  The Fiero has all of the great sports car idiosyncrisies....it's a pain to work on, nobody understands how it works, constantly dipping into your pocket book, and a group of die-hard followers who would go through hell and back to get the "hard to find one with all the great options". Forget bringing back the Fiero, it belongs to our generation.  Let GM build something else that is equally challenging to future car buffs.  Would anyone like to see a return of the Reagan administration?  Let little Joey make his post on some future bulletin board:  <BR>"Hey, if any of you guys happen to have an ion destabilizer laying around I could really use it for my 2015 Pulsar.  I have the Hyper-Drive propulsion with a molecular combustion chamber.  Any help would be great!"  <P>Leave us our Fiero.  It is a true classic.  I love 'em!!!||||reg||1
Z||000028||kel||11-26-1999||01:06 AM||||four50four,<P>Battlestar Galactica was (as stated earlier) a science-fiction series that started in 1978.  It was about a "rag-tag fleet in search of a mythical planet called earth."  It starred Richard Hatch (Apollo), Lorne Greene (Commander Adala- I think), and Dirk Benedict (Starbuck).  The bad guys were cylons (red-eyed robots).  It was a very popular show in it's time.||||reg||1
Z||000029||COUNTIBLIS||11-26-1999||07:20 AM||||Whoa!  Off the subject of the Fiero, I thought I was the only car fanatic/Scfi fanatic on earth!  Great to know that there are more of us!<BR>If you want to know more about Battlestar Galactica "The Second Comming"  goto <A HREF="http://WWW.Battlestargalactica.com" TARGET=_blank>WWW.Battlestargalactica.com</A>   Like I said I know that this is a Fiero forum and a BSG forum so enough of that. By the way I jsut bought a blue 87 se.||||reg||4
